tasks.description:
The repo is public and P2 ports viewer code from a private reference, so the denylist guard must cover every tracked file,
not only tests/fixtures. Write tests/denylist.test.mjs (node:test, zero deps):
- list files with `git ls-files` (run via child_process execFileSync, cwd = repo root);
- exempt docs/design.md (it names a public data platform as a v1.1 roadmap item) and binary files;
- read .private/anonymise-denylist.txt at runtime (skip # comments and blank lines); NEVER inline any term;
- on a hit, fail with "<file>: term #<index>" so CI logs never print a term;
- when the list is absent, call t.skip with a message saying the denylist was not checked.
Keep tests/golden.test.mjs's own check; this one is the repo-wide net.
